# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3): each ask refused alone prints as `<q>: refused: …`, by id (today LOAD-SCENARIO: it names a
# scenario whose file isn't given, L §6.4, §8.3, GD-18), and no `ok`: exit 1. A model with no scenario file; q_z is
# written before q_a, so the lines are in id order, not the text's. q loads and prints nothing.
=== options check exit=1
=== model.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "a model two asks of which name a scenario not given (invented)"

source card "a card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money PLN

def doubled: money PLN = amt + amt at reader

ask q: doubled law 2026-03-01
ask q_z: doubled in raised law 2026-03-01
ask q_a: doubled in lowered law 2026-03-01

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"
=== expect
q_a: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask q_a names lowered, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (model.tally:18)
q_z: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask q_z names raised, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (model.tally:17)
